[{:adr/authoritative_for ["kotoba-lang/wasm-webcomponent: new policy -- kotoba/kototama WASM hosts needing more than a trivial hand-port are authored in ClojureScript and compiled via shadow-cljs :target :esm to a single ES module that runs identically in browser and Node, instead of hand-written per-platform JS. Existing hand-JS modules (actor-host.js/kgraph.js/has-capability.js/kotoba-wasm-element.js) are grandfathered, not retrofitted." "kotoba-lang/wasm-webcomponent src-cljs/kotoba/kami_engine_host.cljs (+ shadow-cljs.edn, compiled src/kami-engine-host.js, test/verify-kami-engine-host.mjs, examples/kami-engine-host/): first implementation under the new policy -- 1:1 port of kami-script-runtime-rs's HostState/EcsStore/KamiHost (14 kami:engine/* host-imports across 4 WASM import modules), parity-verified in Node against the real isekai-network-01-netsurvivors.wasm fixture for 300 ticks (entities=16 shiro-pico=1 ghost=14 beat-spark=1, exact match with kami-script-runtime-rs's own documented Rust/wasmtime trace)." "clojurewasm (cljw) ruled out for WASM-host-providing-imports roles: (1) native-binary-only, does not run in a browser; (2) its WebAssembly FFI is Clojure-calls-wasm only (wasm/load + wasm/call), no documented capability for cljw to provide host-import functions a guest wasm module calls into. Verified via its own README, not assumed." "Addendum 2026-07-08: direction widened to Rust-free including native/windowed targets, not just browser/Node. Concurrent-session work on kotoba-lang/kami-script-runtime-rs (wasmi backend + kami_clj_play native winit+wgpu player) left untouched/unreverted (real, verified, another session's in-progress work), but a documentation-only org-direction notice was added to that crate's README.md/Cargo.toml (commit 4f08f5b42ae7bd4ac0ff91ab0e9c0f80e1b0c068) recording that native desktop targets should go through a webview/Chromium-shell wrapper around the same kami-engine-host/dom-gpu ClojureScript path going forward, not hand-written wgpu/winit. KamiHost's headless-host role (this ADR's actual replacement target, src/lib.rs) verified unaffected by the concurrent session's additions." "Addendum 2 (2026-07-08): Track A (kami-engine-host, removing kami-engine's Rust dependency) declared closed, no further action planned. Proceeding to Track B -- rendering kami-solar-helix-scene's solar helical model via guest-driven WebGPU, kotoba-wasm-runtime-first per CLAUDE.md's priority order, plan at ~/.claude/plans/curious-zooming-sifakis.md. Phase 0 (a synchronous-guest-driven-WebGPU-call technical-risk spike) is next." "Addendum 3 (2026-07-08): Track B Phase 0's capability-contract half landed -- gpu-clear(rgba8: i32) -> 0|-1 registered in kotoba-core-contracts (id 226, kotoba-core-contracts#5), one packed 0xRRGGBBAA i32 instead of the plan's sketched 3-param (r,g,b) shape (a deliberate ABI simplification during implementation, matching the (scalar-in) -> status-out convention every other non-buffer import here uses). NOT yet landed and NOT claimed as done: the actual browser host implementation (device/adapter/canvas setup + the gpu_clear HostFunction, authored in ClojureScript per this ADR's own Decision, not hand-JS), a minimal .kotoba guest, and Phase 0's real acceptance criterion -- a claude-in-chrome screenshot confirming the canvas genuinely clears to the requested color in a live browser tab. Phase 0 remains open until verified against a real browser, not just declared in an EDN table." "Addendum 4 (2026-07-08): Track B Phase 0 CLOSED, browser-verified. Addendum 3's outstanding half is now landed: kotoba-lang/wasm-webcomponent src-cljs/kotoba/gpu_clear_host.cljs -> src/gpu-clear-host.js (shadow-cljs :target :esm :advanced, ClojureScript-authored per this ADR's Decision, not hand-JS -- required unchecked-get/js-invoke throughout to survive :advanced property renaming against externs-less WebGPU calls) + demo_gpu_clear.kotoba (real kotoba wasm emit after bumping kotoba-lang/kotoba's kotoba-core-contracts pin to e5bc820 -- kotoba-lang/kotoba commit 3ba5f607, 146 tests/786 assertions green). Real browser verification via claude-in-chrome against GitHub Pages (https://kotoba-lang.github.io/wasm-webcomponent/examples/gpu-clear/, enabled specifically because both a local static server and a claude.ai Artifact iframe preview were unreachable/uninspectable from this sandboxed session): screenshot confirms canvas fully opaque red, #out reads 'main() -> 0 (0 = gpu_clear succeeded)'. Phase 0's actual risk -- guest-driven WebGPU as a genuinely synchronous host-import -- is confirmed against a live browser, not just argued from spec. Track B Phase 1 (cos/sin builtins, gpu-set-instance-transform/gpu-set-camera/gpu-draw-frame, kami-solar-helix-scene position-math port, 9-body vertical slice) is unblocked." "Addendum 5 (2026-07-08): proceeding to Track B Phase 1 -- .kotoba cos/sin builtins, gpu-set-instance-transform/gpu-set-camera/gpu-draw-frame capability set, kami-solar-helix-scene position-math port to .kotoba, 9-body (Sun + 8 planets) vertical-slice render with heliocentric/galactic frame toggle, browser-verified per Phase 0's precedent." "Addendum 6 (2026-07-08): Track B Phase 1 CLOSED, 9/9 bodies rendered and browser-verified. Shipped f32 support in kotoba-lang/kotoba's compiler (commit 05088a18, not in the original sketch -- host-import ABI was i32/i64-only; also fixed a latent wasm-exec/call-main f32-decoding bug this surfaced). Capabilities: math/cos, math/sin, gpu/set-position(body-id,x,y,z), gpu/draw-frame -- scalar-only by design (no guest-constructed matrix/camera; .kotoba has no vector/matrix type or loops-beyond-recursion), not the instance-transform/camera shape Addendum 5 sketched (kotoba-core-contracts commit 3e60ae6, kotoba-lang/kotoba pin bumped to b7f8427c, 152 tests green). Guest demo_solar_helix.kotoba: static single-frame render (t=45 days fixed, sqrt-scaled orbital radii, real cos/sin/f32sqrt) -- not yet animated, not yet the galactic-frame toggle (explicitly deferred, see Follow-up). Host solar_render_host.cljs: procedural UV sphere mesh, hand-written mat4 math (no external dep), one draw call per body, fixed camera, WGSL shader. Two real bugs found only via live-browser verification (both invisible to structural/compile checks): (1) host initially missing cos/sin wiring -> LinkError before main() ran; (2) after fixing that, main() succeeded but nothing rendered -- root cause was a single shared uniform buffer aliased across all 9 recorded draw calls (queue.writeBuffer executes immediately, pass.drawIndexed only records until queue.submit()), fixed with one buffer+bind-group per body slot. Also needed a camera pull-back after an initial verified render showed only 7/9 bodies (Uranus/Neptune frustum-clipped). Verified via GitHub Pages + claude-in-chrome, final screenshot: all 9 bodies visible, correctly colored/sized/ordered inner-to-outer." "Addendum 7 (2026-07-08): maturity/coverage pass (kotoba-lang/wasm-webcomponent commit 1a74d4e, merged to main as ac0db24). Phase 0/1's two ClojureScript hosts (gpu_clear_host.cljs, solar_render_host.cljs) had zero direct unit-test coverage of their own pure logic -- every mat4/vec3/sphere-mesh/bit-unpacking helper was defn- (private) and only ever exercised transitively through a live WebGPU browser render. Promoted unpack-rgba8, mat4-multiply/mat4-perspective/mat4-look-at/mat4-translation-scale, vec3-normalize/vec3-sub/vec3-cross/vec3-dot, and build-sphere-mesh to defn (public) + shadow-cljs.edn :exports entries; deleted mat4-identity as confirmed-unused dead code; changed build-sphere-mesh's return from a Clojure map to a plain JS object so its fields survive :advanced Closure renaming and are readable from a Node test. Added test/verify-gpu-clear-host.mjs (7 assertions) and test/verify-solar-render-host.mjs (17 assertions), an npm test runner covering all 8 verify-*.mjs files, compile:/release: package.json scripts for the two builds (previously only kami-engine-host had them), and README.md ## Files/## Run the tests coverage for both modules and their examples/ dirs, none of which existed since Phase 0/1 shipped. Does NOT add coverage for the actual WebGPU draw path (pipeline/bind-groups/queue.submit timing, where both Addendum 6 bugs were found) -- that still requires a real browser, unchanged by this pass." "Addendum 8 (2026-07-08): Track B Phase 1 follow-up CLOSED -- animation + heliocentric/galactic view toggle, both real-GPU-verified. Two new capabilities (kotoba-core-contracts commit 2d6983a, ids 231/232): time/now-days() -> f32 (host-owned wrapped simulated day count, wall-clock-driven) and render/galactic-frame() -> i32 (host-owned view-toggle boolean). kotoba-lang/kotoba pin bumped to it (commit 610f80f, 184 tests green). A real, previously-latent compiler bug found and fixed en route (kotoba-lang/kotoba commit edb768f): compile-wasm-expr's `if` hardcoded the WASM if block's own result-type byte to i32 regardless of the branches' actual type -- undetected until this session's f32-typed `(if gal (f32* ...) (f32 0.0))` hit it, Chicory rejecting the bytecode with a stack type-mismatch; fixed by reading the block-type byte from compiled-result-type via wasm-valtypes (same latent bug affected i64-typed if too, same fix). A second bug fixed alongside: kotoba.wasm-exec/stub-host-function's valtype map had no :f32 entry, NullPointerException'ing on any f32-result host-import stubbed under `kotoba wasm run`. Guest (demo_solar_helix.kotoba) ports galactic-frame-position-au's tilt+forward-drift transform 1:1 (illustrative forward-per-day constant calibrated to Earth's real ~7.4x pitch/circumference ratio); a real sign bug (forward moving bodies toward the fixed camera instead of away, found via live-browser verification) was fixed before landing. Host (solar_render_host.cljs) drives now_days/galactic_frame off a wall-clock-derived, JS-wrapped clock; setFixedNowDays exposed as a test-only determinism hook. Verified three independent ways: (1) a GPU-free numerical sweep of the guest's own math across the full now-days range, cross-checked against kotoba-lang/kotoba's own Chicory JVM tooling; (2) interactive real-browser screenshots confirming correct rendering at load and immediately after toggling, though sustained multi-second live animation intermittently went blank in the sandboxed browser-automation tool used for that verification -- investigated (not shrugged off) and root-caused to that tool's own repeated WebGPU device/canvas churn, not the shipped code (a fresh isolated canvas driven through the identical host kept rendering correctly for hundreds of frames after the page's own canvas had already gone black); (3) headless real-GPU CI (test/render/verify-render-solar-helix.mjs, built on a concurrent session's new Playwright-based test/render/ harness) with a new setFixedNowDays/?test_fixed_t query-param determinism hook, verifying both view modes via exact landmark pixel positions/colors in a single real-macOS-GPU-rendered frame. Landed across kotoba-core-contracts/kotoba/wasm-webcomponent (merged 39692cd, itself requiring a real merge-conflict resolution against a concurrent session's test/render/ infrastructure that landed mid-branch). Remaining Addendum 6 Follow-up items (cullMode 'back', guest-controlled camera/color) still explicitly deferred, not attempted this pass."], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "kotoba-lang-wasm-webcomponent-cljs-esm-host", :adr/related ["adr-2607072700-kotoba-lang-kami-solar-helix-scene" "adr-2607061630-kototama-browser-wasm-aot-webcomponent" "adr-2607061850-kotoba-lang-wasm-webcomponent-library-extraction" "adr-2607062400"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607078000-kotoba-lang-wasm-webcomponent-cljs-esm-host", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-08", :adr/body "see 2607078000-kotoba-lang-wasm-webcomponent-cljs-esm-host.md", :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"], :adr/artifacts "{:wasm-webcomponent \"kotoba-lang/wasm-webcomponent -- kami-engine-host + gpu-clear-host + solar-render-host cljs/esm ports; solar-helix animates continuously with a heliocentric/galactic view toggle, verified via GPU-free math sweep + interactive real-browser screenshots + headless real-GPU CI (test/render/verify-render-solar-helix.mjs, both view modes) (commit 39692cd); gpu-clear-host/solar-render-host pure logic (bit-unpacking, mat4/vec3 math, sphere-mesh generation) unit-tested via test/verify-gpu-clear-host.mjs + test/verify-solar-render-host.mjs (commit 1a74d4e, merged ac0db24)\", :kami-script-runtime-rs \"kotoba-lang/kami-script-runtime-rs -- docs-only org-direction notice, commit 4f08f5b42ae7bd4ac0ff91ab0e9c0f80e1b0c068, no code changed\", :kotoba-core-contracts \"kotoba-lang/kotoba-core-contracts -- gpu-clear (id 226) + math/cos + math/sin + gpu/set-position + gpu/draw-frame + time/now-days (id 231) + render/galactic-frame (id 232) capabilities registered (commit 2d6983a), all consumed end-to-end and browser-verified\", :kotoba \"kotoba-lang/kotoba -- real f32 support added to the compiler (commit 05088a18) + wasm-exec f32-decoding fix; `if`'s WASM block-type byte fixed to reflect the branches' actual result type instead of a hardcoded i32, + stub-host-function's missing :f32 valtype entry fixed (commit edb768f); kotoba-core-contracts pin bumped to 2d6983a (commit 610f80f), 184 tests green; demo_solar_helix.wasm compiled via real kotoba wasm emit\"}", :adr/date "2026-07-07", :db/id -1, :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607078000: wasm-webcomponent's zero-build-step hand-JS host policy is superseded — kotoba/kototama WASM hosts are authored in ClojureScript, compiled once, run everywhere (browser + Node)"}]